{title: Now Thank We All Our God}
{title_ko: 다 감사드리세}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 66장}
{artist: Martin Rinkart, tr. Catherine Winkworth / Johann Crüger}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{key_original: F}
{tempo: 88}
{time: 4/4}
{score: now-thank-we-all-our-god.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Now thank we all our [D]God
With [Em]heart and hands and [C]voices
[G]Who wondrous things hath [D]done
In [Em]whom His world re[D]joices
[G]Who from our mothers' [D]arms
Hath [Em]blessed us on our [C]way
With [G]countless gifts of [D]love
And [C]still is [D]ours to[G]day
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]O may this bounteous [D]God
Through [Em]all our life be [C]near us
With [G]ever joyful [D]hearts
And [Em]blessed peace to [D]cheer us
And [G]keep us in His [D]grace
And [Em]guide us when per[C]plexed
And [G]free us from all [D]ills
In [C]this world [D]and the [G]next
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]All praise and thanks to [D]God
The [Em]Father now be [C]given
The [G]Son, and Him who [D]reigns
With [Em]them in highest [D]heaven
The [G]one eternal [D]God
Whom [Em]earth and heaven a[C]dore
For [G]thus it was, is [D]now
And [C]shall be [D]ever[G]more
{end_of_verse}
